Package: com.qoij.tunefetch
Name: TuneFetch
Depends: preferenceloader, firmware (>= 6.0)
Description: Download music on your PC, receive it on this iPhone
 TuneFetch turns your iPhone into a remote
 control for a download program on your PC.
 Paste YouTube links or type song names in
 the TuneFetch app. Your PC downloads them
 with yt-dlp and sends the finished files
 to a folder on this iPhone over Wi-Fi.
 .
 Features:
  * MP3, M4A, AAC, WAV and MP4 video
  * FLAC, Opus, OGG, MKV, WebM (optional)
  * Queue with progress, cancel and retry
  * Cover art and playlists
  * Files go to /var/mobile/Media/music
 .
 How to set it up:
  1. Run TuneFetch Host on your PC
  2. Press "QR code" in the host window
  3. Open the TuneFetch app, Settings,
     tap "Scan QR code from the host"
  4. Tap Test connection
 (or type the PC's IP address and the
 access code yourself)
 .
 Needs a PC with Python 3.9+ on the same
 Wi-Fi. Songs do not appear in the Music
 app; open them with a file manager or a
 player that reads folders.
